************************************************************************
*
* Tachyon Webmail — Nextcloud integration
*
* https://github.com/kimusan/Tachyon
*
************************************************************************

REQUIREMENTS
------------
- Nextcloud 26 or later (tested up to 34)
- PHP 8.2 or later
- PHP extensions: mbstring, zlib


FRESH INSTALL
-------------
1. In Nextcloud Admin → Apps, find "Tachyon" and click Enable.
   (Or install manually by placing the tachyon/ directory in apps/.)

2. Go to Nextcloud Admin → Additional settings → Tachyon webmail.

3. Click the link to the Tachyon admin panel. The generated admin
   password is in:
     <nextcloud-data>/appdata_tachyon/_data_/_default_/admin_password.txt
   Change it after first login.

4. In the Tachyon admin panel, configure your mail domain under
   Domains (IMAP/SMTP host, port, and security settings).


MIGRATING FROM SNAPPYMAIL
--------------------------
Tachyon is a separate Nextcloud app (app ID: tachyon). It cannot be
installed by extracting files on top of an existing SnappyMail
installation — doing so leaves the old app registered and causes a
fatal error on startup.

Correct migration steps:

1. In Nextcloud Admin → Apps, DISABLE the SnappyMail app.
2. Remove the old app directory from your server:
     rm -rf /path/to/nextcloud/apps/snappymail
3. Install Tachyon from the app store, or place the tachyon/
   directory in apps/.
4. Enable Tachyon in Admin → Apps.

Your existing mail data is kept automatically. Tachyon checks both
appdata_tachyon/ and appdata_snappymail/ and uses whichever exists,
so no data migration is needed.


AUTO-LOGIN
----------
Tachyon can log users in automatically using their Nextcloud
credentials. Enable one of these options in Admin → Additional
settings → Tachyon webmail:

- "Auto-login using Nextcloud username" — uses the NC username as
  the IMAP login name.
- "Auto-login using Nextcloud email address" — uses the email
  address set in the user's profile.

Users can also set a custom email/password under their personal
settings if they use different credentials for their mail server.


STUCK IN MAINTENANCE MODE
--------------------------
If Tachyon gets stuck in maintenance mode, run from your Nextcloud
root:
  php occ maintenance:mode --off
  php occ app:disable tachyon
  php occ app:enable tachyon
